.env
data/

# Key material for the connector — real secp256k1/ed25519 secrets, generated by
# README.md's own steps and mounted into the container. Wildcarded rather than
# listed by name so a re-derived or additional key cannot reintroduce the gap by
# being named slightly differently.
#
# The same rule catches the two secrets a STATION holds that no other node in
# the fleet does:
#   * stream.key       — the broadcaster's stream key. It is what stops anyone
#                        else broadcasting as this station, it is checked on
#                        the RTMP publish, and it is mounted, never baked into
#                        an image and never a default in code.
#   * ingest-tls.key   — the private half of the RTMPS certificate the origin
#                        terminates its own ingest TLS with.
*.key
*.secret
*.pem

# The public half of the RTMPS certificate. Not secret, but it is per box and
# per hostname, so it does not belong in a repository every broadcaster clones.
ingest-tls.crt

# The operator surface's credentials (connector.toml [operator]). The bearer
# token is a secret outright; the allowlist is public halves but per box, so
# neither belongs in a repository every broadcaster clones.
operator-bearer.token
operator-write.keys
